      "stageRecord": "The overt relativizer الذي is analyzed as a relative C selecting the completed relative T domain. A silent operator is externally merged at the relative edge and binds the object pronoun inside اشتراه. This is a resumptive derivation, not extraction of الكتاب or movement of the object pronoun: the operator has no lower copy, and the pronounced pronoun remains the verb's internal argument. The resulting relative clause is adjoined to the nominal projection, restricting the book to the one Samer bought. الذي matches the definite masculine singular nominal head. Independently, a silent declarative C closes the main finite clause. The two object clitics are distinct syntactic objects: relative binding is established here, while the main-clause clitic awaits its topic antecedent.",
      "statement": "Complete the resumptive relative clause and attach it to the nominal head.",
